1
00:00:00,180 --> 00:00:03,779
part 3 chapter 3.

2
00:00:03,779 --> 00:00:07,740
There are three stages in your reintegration said O'Brien There is

3
00:00:07,740 --> 00:00:11,457
learning, there is understanding, and there is acceptance.

4
00:00:11,457 --> 00:00:15,020
It is time for you to enter upon the second stage.'

5
00:00:15,020 --> 00:00:18,599
As always, Winston was lying flat on his back.

6
00:00:18,599 --> 00:00:21,180
But of late his bonds were looser.

7
00:00:21,180 --> 00:00:24,718
They still held him to the bed, but he could move his knees a little and could

8
00:00:24,718 --> 00:00:28,439
turn his head from side to side and raise his arms from the elbow.

9
00:00:28,439 --> 00:00:32,759
The dial, also, had grown to be less of a terror. He could evade its pangs if he

10
00:00:32,759 --> 00:00:36,297
was quick-witted enough: it was chiefly when he showed stupidity

11
00:00:36,297 --> 00:00:38,637
that her brand pulled the lever.

12
00:00:38,637 --> 00:00:41,878
Sometimes they got through a whole session without use of the dial.

13
00:00:41,878 --> 00:00:45,957
He could not remember how many sessions there had been. The whole process seemed

14
00:00:45,957 --> 00:00:51,119
to stretch out over a long, indefinite time— —weeks, possibly— —and the intervals

15
00:00:51,119 --> 00:00:56,340
between the sessions might sometimes have been days, sometimes only an hour or two.

16
00:00:56,340 --> 00:01:00,297
'As you lie there,' said a brand you have often wondered— —you have even asked me—

17
00:01:00,297 --> 00:01:04,919
—why the Ministry of Love should expend so much time and trouble on you.

18
00:01:04,919 --> 00:01:07,860
And when you are free you have puzzled by what was essentially the same

19
00:01:07,860 --> 00:01:12,419
question. You could grasp the mechanics of the society you lived in, but not its

20
00:01:12,419 --> 00:01:13,977
underlying motives.

21
00:01:13,977 --> 00:01:20,040
Do you remember writing in your diary, "I understand how: I do not understand why"?

22
00:01:20,040 --> 00:01:23,939
It was when you thought about "why" that you doubted your own sanity. You have

23
00:01:23,939 --> 00:01:28,259
read the book, Goldstein's book, or parts of it, at least. Did it tell you anything

24
00:01:28,259 --> 00:01:30,898
that you did not know already?'

25
00:01:30,898 --> 00:01:33,540
'You have read it?' said Winston.

26
00:01:33,540 --> 00:01:34,977
'I wrote it.

27
00:01:34,977 --> 00:01:40,860
That is to say, I collaborated in writing it. No book is produced individually, as you know.'

28
00:01:40,860 --> 00:01:42,957
'Is it true, what it says?'

29
00:01:42,957 --> 00:01:47,819
'As description, yes. The program it sets forth is nonsense. The secret

30
00:01:47,819 --> 00:01:51,718
accumulation of knowledge— —a gradual spread of enlightenment— —ultimately a

31
00:01:51,718 --> 00:01:56,580
proletarian rebellion— —the overthrow of the Party. You foresaw yourself that that

32
00:01:56,580 --> 00:01:58,020
was what it would say.

33
00:01:58,020 --> 00:02:04,080
It is all nonsense. The proletarians will never revolt, not in a thousand years or a million.

34
00:02:04,080 --> 00:02:07,860
They cannot. I do not have to tell you the reason: you know it already.

35
00:02:07,860 --> 00:02:12,240
If you have ever cherished any dreams of violent insurrection, you must abandon them.

36
00:02:12,240 --> 00:02:18,000
There is no way in which the Party can be overthrown. The rule of the Party is forever

37
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:21,360
Make that the starting point of your thoughts.'

38
00:02:21,360 --> 00:02:25,500
He came closer to the bed forever he repeated.

39
00:02:25,500 --> 00:02:29,218
'And now let us get back to the question of "how" and "why".

40
00:02:29,218 --> 00:02:33,000
You understand well enough how the Party maintains itself in power.

41
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:36,718
Now tell me why we cling to power. What is our motive?

42
00:02:36,718 --> 00:02:43,159
Why should we want power? Go on, speak,' he added as Winston remained silent.

43
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:46,797
Nevertheless Winston did not speak for another moment or two

44
00:02:46,797 --> 00:02:51,540
the feeling of weariness had overwhelmed him. The faint, mad gleam of enthusiasm

45
00:02:51,540 --> 00:02:53,759
had come back into O'Brien's face.

46
00:02:53,759 --> 00:02:57,477
He knew in advance what O'Brien would say. That the Party did not seek power

47
00:02:57,477 --> 00:03:00,477
for its own ends, but only for the good of the majority.

48
00:03:00,477 --> 00:03:04,439
That it sought power because men in the mass were frail cowardly creatures who

49
00:03:04,439 --> 00:03:08,398
could not endure liberty or face the truth, and must be ruled over and

50
00:03:08,398 --> 00:03:12,240
systematically deceived by others who are stronger than themselves. That the

51
00:03:12,240 --> 00:03:15,718
choice for mankind lay between freedom and happiness, and that, for the great

52
00:03:15,718 --> 00:03:17,520
bulk of mankind, happiness was better.

53
00:03:17,520 --> 00:03:22,439
That the Party was the eternal guardian of the week a dedicated sect doing evil

54
00:03:22,439 --> 00:03:26,580
that good might come, sacrificing its own happiness to that of others.

55
00:03:26,580 --> 00:03:30,000
The terrible thing, thought Winston, the terrible thing was that when O'Brien

56
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:31,860
said this he would believe it.

57
00:03:31,860 --> 00:03:36,779
You could see it in his face a brand new everything. A thousand times better than

58
00:03:36,779 --> 00:03:41,457
Winston he knew what the world was really like, in what degradation the mass of human

59
00:03:41,457 --> 00:03:45,659
beings lived and by what lies and the barbarities the Party kept them there.

60
00:03:45,659 --> 00:03:49,860
He had understood it all, weighed it all, and it made no difference: all was

61
00:03:49,860 --> 00:03:52,200
justified by the ultimate purpose.

62
00:03:52,200 --> 00:03:56,218
What can you do, thought Winston, against the lunatic who is more intelligent than

63
00:03:56,218 --> 00:04:01,439
yourself, who gives your arguments a fair hearing and then simply persists in his lunacy?

64
00:04:01,439 --> 00:04:05,580
'You were ruling over us for our own good,' he said feebly. 'You believe that human

65
00:04:05,580 --> 00:04:09,477
beings are not fitted to govern themselves, and therefore———' He started and

66
00:04:09,477 --> 00:04:13,860
almost cried out. A pang of pain had shot through his body. O'Brien had pushed the

67
00:04:13,860 --> 00:04:17,040
lever of the dial up to 35.

68
00:04:17,040 --> 00:04:19,797
That was stupid, Winston, stupid!' he said.

69
00:04:19,797 --> 00:04:22,977
'You should know better than to say a thing like that.'

70
00:04:22,977 --> 00:04:27,599
He pulled the lever back and continued: 'Now I will tell you the answer to my

71
00:04:27,599 --> 00:04:29,637
question. It is this.

72
00:04:29,637 --> 00:04:33,779
The Party seeks power entirely for its own sake. We are not interested in the

73
00:04:33,779 --> 00:04:37,020
good of others; we are interested solely in power.

74
00:04:37,020 --> 00:04:42,540
Not wealth or luxury or long life or happiness: only power, pure power.

75
00:04:42,540 --> 00:04:45,957
What pure power means you will understand presently.

76
00:04:45,957 --> 00:04:50,759
We are different from all the oligarchies of the past, in that we know what we are doing.

77
00:04:50,759 --> 00:04:55,558
All the others, even those who resembled ourselves, were cowards and hypocrites.

78
00:04:55,558 --> 00:04:58,919
The German Nazis and the Russian Communists came very close to us in

79
00:04:58,919 --> 00:05:03,360
their methods, but they never had the courage to recognize their own motives.

80
00:05:03,360 --> 00:05:06,540
They pretended, perhaps they even believed, that they had seized power

81
00:05:06,540 --> 00:05:10,558
unwillingly and for a limited time, and that just around the corner they lay a

82
00:05:10,558 --> 00:05:13,797
paradise where human beings would be free and equal.

83
00:05:13,797 --> 00:05:18,477
We are not like that. We know that no one ever ceases power with the intention of

84
00:05:18,477 --> 00:05:19,919
relinquishing it.

85
00:05:19,919 --> 00:05:22,619
Power is not a means, it is an end.

86
00:05:22,619 --> 00:05:26,819
One does not establish a dictatorship in order to safeguard a revolution; one

87
00:05:26,819 --> 00:05:30,058
makes the revolution in order to establish the dictatorship.

88
00:05:30,058 --> 00:05:32,759
The object of persecution is persecution.

89
00:05:32,759 --> 00:05:37,319
The object of torture is torture. The object of power is power.

90
00:05:37,319 --> 00:05:41,180
Now do you begin to understand me?'

91
00:05:41,340 --> 00:05:45,297
Winston was struck, as he had been struck before, by the tiredness of O'Brien's

92
00:05:45,297 --> 00:05:49,797
face. It was strong and fleshy and brutal, it was full of intelligence and a sort

93
00:05:49,797 --> 00:05:52,919
of controlled passion before which he felt himself helpless;

94
00:05:52,919 --> 00:05:58,680
but it was tired. There were pouches under the eyes, the skin sagged from the cheekbones.

95
00:05:58,680 --> 00:06:03,540
O'Brien leaned over him, deliberately bringing the worn face nearer.

96
00:06:03,540 --> 00:06:07,977
'You are thinking,' he said, 'that my face is old and tired. You were thinking that I

97
00:06:07,977 --> 00:06:12,000
talk of power, and yet I am not even able to prevent the decay of my own body.

98
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:15,779
Can you not understand, Winston, that the individual is only a cell?

99
00:06:15,779 --> 00:06:19,860
The weariness of the cell is the Vigor of the organism. Do you die when you cut

100
00:06:19,860 --> 00:06:21,840
your fingernails?'

101
00:06:21,840 --> 00:06:27,419
He turned away from the bed and began strolling up and down again, one hand in his pocket.

102
00:06:27,419 --> 00:06:32,398
'We are the priests of power,' he said. 'God is power. But at present power is only a

103
00:06:32,398 --> 00:06:36,297
word so far as you are concerned. It is time for you to gather some idea of what

104
00:06:36,297 --> 00:06:37,558
power means.

105
00:06:37,558 --> 00:06:40,977
The first thing you must realize is that power is collective.

106
00:06:40,977 --> 00:06:45,119
The individual only has power in so far as he ceases to be an individual.

107
00:06:45,119 --> 00:06:49,740
You know the Party slogan: "Freedom is Slavery." Has it ever occurred to you that

108
00:06:49,740 --> 00:06:51,180
it is reversible?

109
00:06:51,180 --> 00:06:53,099
Slavery is freedom.

110
00:06:53,099 --> 00:06:58,558
Alone— —free— —the human being is always defeated. It must be so, because every

111
00:06:58,558 --> 00:07:02,398
human being is doomed to die, which is the greatest of all failures.

112
00:07:02,398 --> 00:07:06,360
But if he can make complete, utter submission, if he can escape from his

113
00:07:06,360 --> 00:07:10,977
identity, if he can merge himself in the Party so that he is the Party, then he is

114
00:07:10,977 --> 00:07:12,779
all-powerful and immortal.

115
00:07:12,779 --> 00:07:17,878
The second thing for you to realize is that power is power of human beings. Over

116
00:07:17,878 --> 00:07:20,457
the body— —but, above all, over the mind.

117
00:07:20,457 --> 00:07:24,119
Power over matter— —external reality, as you would call it— —is not important.

118
00:07:24,119 --> 00:07:28,200
Already our control over matter is absolute.'

119
00:07:28,200 --> 00:07:32,159
For a moment Winston ignored the dial. He made a violent effort to raise himself

120
00:07:32,159 --> 00:07:36,840
into a sitting position, and merely succeeded in wrenching his body painfully.

121
00:07:36,840 --> 00:07:40,860
'But how can you control matter?' he burst out. 'You don't even control the climate

122
00:07:40,860 --> 00:07:42,419
or the law of gravity.

123
00:07:42,419 --> 00:07:47,457
And there are disease, pain, death———' O'Brien silenced him by a movement of

124
00:07:47,457 --> 00:07:52,319
his hand. 'We control matter because we control the mind. Reality is inside the

125
00:07:52,319 --> 00:07:55,319
skull. You will learn by degrees, Winston.

126
00:07:55,319 --> 00:07:57,200
There is nothing that we could not do.

127
00:07:57,200 --> 00:08:02,340
Invisibility, levitation— —anything. I could float off this floor like a soap bubble

128
00:08:02,340 --> 00:08:03,540
if I wish to.

129
00:08:03,540 --> 00:08:06,360
I do not wish to, because the Party does not wish it.

130
00:08:06,360 --> 00:08:10,619
You must get rid of those 19th century ideas about the laws of Nature. We make

131
00:08:10,619 --> 00:08:12,500
the laws of Nature.'

132
00:08:12,500 --> 00:08:17,580
'But you do not you're not even masters of this planet. What about Eurasia and

133
00:08:17,580 --> 00:08:20,700
East Asia You have not conquered them yet.'

134
00:08:20,700 --> 00:08:24,957
'Unimportant. We shall conquer them when it suits us. And if we did not, what

135
00:08:24,957 --> 00:08:30,360
difference would it make? We can shut them out of existence. Oceania is the world.'

136
00:08:30,360 --> 00:08:35,700
'But the world itself is only a speck of dust. And man is tiny— —helpless! How long

137
00:08:35,700 --> 00:08:40,200
has he been in existence? For millions of years the earth was uninhabited.'

138
00:08:40,200 --> 00:08:45,957
'Nonsense. The earth is as old as we are, no older. How could it be older? Nothing

139
00:08:45,957 --> 00:08:48,898
exists except through human consciousness.'

140
00:08:48,898 --> 00:08:53,700
'But the rocks are full of the bones of extinct animals— —mammoths and mastodons

141
00:08:53,700 --> 00:08:58,500
and enormous reptiles which lived here long before man was ever heard of.'

142
00:08:58,500 --> 00:09:00,840
'Have you ever seen those bones, Winston?

143
00:09:00,840 --> 00:09:06,898
Of course not 19th century biologists invented them. Before man there was nothing.

144
00:09:06,898 --> 00:09:13,200
After man, if he could come to an end, there would be nothing. Outside man there is nothing.'

145
00:09:13,200 --> 00:09:15,119
'But the whole universe is outside us.

146
00:09:15,119 --> 00:09:19,439
Look at the stars! Some of them are a million light years away.

147
00:09:19,439 --> 00:09:24,599
They are out of our reach forever What are the stars?' said O'Brien

148
00:09:24,599 --> 00:09:28,680
indifferently. 'They are bits of fire a few kilometers away. We could reach them

149
00:09:28,680 --> 00:09:29,878
if we wanted to.

150
00:09:29,878 --> 00:09:34,740
Or we could blot them out. The earth is the center of the universe. The sun and

151
00:09:34,740 --> 00:09:37,378
the stars go around it.'

152
00:09:37,378 --> 00:09:39,419
Winston made another convulsive movement.

153
00:09:39,419 --> 00:09:41,878
This time he did not say anything.

154
00:09:41,878 --> 00:09:46,558
O'Brien continued as though answering a spoken objection:

155
00:09:46,558 --> 00:09:50,520
'For certain purposes, of course, that is not true. When we navigate to the ocean,

156
00:09:50,520 --> 00:09:54,360
or when we predict an eclipse, we often find it convenient to assume that the

157
00:09:54,360 --> 00:09:58,860
earth goes round to the sun and that the stars are millions upon millions of kilometers away.

158
00:09:58,860 --> 00:10:04,137
But what of it? Do you suppose it is beyond us to produce a dual system of astronomy?

159
00:10:04,137 --> 00:10:07,439
The stars can be near or distant, according as we need them.

160
00:10:07,439 --> 00:10:12,898
Do you suppose our mathematicians are unequal to that? Have you forgotten doublethink?'

161
00:10:12,898 --> 00:10:15,477
Winston shrank back upon the bed.

162
00:10:15,477 --> 00:10:19,319
Whatever he said, the swift answer crushed him like a bludgeon.

163
00:10:19,319 --> 00:10:22,619
And yet he knew, he knew, that he was in the right.

164
00:10:22,619 --> 00:10:27,540
The belief that nothing exists outside your own mind— —surely there must be some way of

165
00:10:27,540 --> 00:10:29,520
demonstrating that it was false?

166
00:10:29,520 --> 00:10:32,939
Had it not been exposed long ago as a fallacy?

167
00:10:32,939 --> 00:10:35,759
There was even a name for it, which he had forgotten.

168
00:10:35,759 --> 00:10:40,977
A faint smile twitched to the corners of her Brian's mouth as he looked down at him.

169
00:10:40,977 --> 00:10:45,000
'I told you, Winston,' he said, 'that metaphysics is not your strong point.

170
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:47,700
The word you are trying to think of is solipsism.

171
00:10:47,700 --> 00:10:52,319
But you're mistaken. This is not solipsism. Collective solipsism, if you

172
00:10:52,319 --> 00:10:56,457
like. But that is a different thing: in fact, the opposite thing.

173
00:10:56,457 --> 00:11:00,779
All this is a digression,' he added in a different tone. 'The real power, the power

174
00:11:00,779 --> 00:11:05,520
we have to fight for night and today is not power over things, but over men.'

175
00:11:05,520 --> 00:11:09,718
He paused, and for a moment assumed again his heir of a schoolmaster questioning a

176
00:11:09,718 --> 00:11:15,419
promising pupil: 'How does one man assert his power over another, Winston?'

177
00:11:15,419 --> 00:11:16,919
Winston thought.

178
00:11:16,919 --> 00:11:19,259
'By making him suffer,' he said.

179
00:11:19,259 --> 00:11:22,137
'Exactly. By making him suffer.

180
00:11:22,137 --> 00:11:24,119
Obedience is not enough.

181
00:11:24,119 --> 00:11:27,180
Unless he is suffering, how can you be sure that he is obeying your will and

182
00:11:27,180 --> 00:11:28,619
not his own?

183
00:11:28,619 --> 00:11:31,919
Power is in inflicting pain and humiliation.

184
00:11:31,919 --> 00:11:35,398
Power is in tearing human minds to pieces and putting them together again

185
00:11:35,398 --> 00:11:37,797
in new shapes of your own choosing.

186
00:11:37,797 --> 00:11:42,119
Do you begin to see, then, what kind of world we are creating? It is the exact

187
00:11:42,119 --> 00:11:46,080
opposite of the stupid hedonistic Utopias that the old reformers imagined.

188
00:11:46,080 --> 00:11:49,919
A world of fear into treachery and a torment, a world of trampling and being

189
00:11:49,919 --> 00:11:56,040
trampled upon, a world which will grow not less but more merciless as it refines itself.

190
00:11:56,040 --> 00:11:59,637
Progress in our world will be progressed towards more pain.

191
00:11:59,637 --> 00:12:03,779
The old civilizations claimed that they were founded on love or justice.

192
00:12:03,779 --> 00:12:08,700
Ours is founded upon hatred. In our world there will be no emotions except fear,

193
00:12:08,700 --> 00:12:11,040
rage, triumph and self-abasement.

194
00:12:11,040 --> 00:12:14,218
Everything else we shall destroy— —everything.

195
00:12:14,218 --> 00:12:17,457
Already we are breaking down the habits of thought which have survived from

196
00:12:17,457 --> 00:12:21,477
before the Revolution. We have cut the links between child and parent, and

197
00:12:21,477 --> 00:12:25,020
between man and man, and between man and woman.

198
00:12:25,020 --> 00:12:28,740
No one dares trust a wife or a child or a friend any longer.

199
00:12:28,740 --> 00:12:32,878
But in the future there will be no wives and no friends. Children will be taken

200
00:12:32,878 --> 00:12:37,378
from their mothers at birth, as one takes eggs from a hen. The sex instinct will be

201
00:12:37,378 --> 00:12:42,599
eradicated. Procreation will be an annual formality like the renewal of a ration card.

202
00:12:42,599 --> 00:12:46,680
We shall abolish the orgasm. Our neurologists are at work upon it now.

203
00:12:46,680 --> 00:12:51,360
There will be no loyalty, except loyalty towards the Party. There will be no love,

204
00:12:51,360 --> 00:12:55,500
except the love of Big Brother. There will be no laughter, except the laugh of

205
00:12:55,500 --> 00:12:57,718
triumph over a defeated enemy.

206
00:12:57,718 --> 00:13:02,099
There will be no art, no literature, no science. When we are omnipotent we shall

207
00:13:02,099 --> 00:13:03,840
have no more need of science.

208
00:13:03,840 --> 00:13:07,740
There will be no distinction between beauty and ugliness. There will be no

209
00:13:07,740 --> 00:13:10,919
curiosity, no enjoyment of the process of life.

210
00:13:10,919 --> 00:13:13,558
All competing pleasures will be destroyed.

211
00:13:13,558 --> 00:13:18,119
But always— —do not forget this, Winston— —always there will be the intoxication of

212
00:13:18,119 --> 00:13:21,957
power, constantly increasing and constantly growing subtler.

213
00:13:21,957 --> 00:13:25,797
Always, at every moment, there will be the thrill of victory, the sensation of

214
00:13:25,797 --> 00:13:28,200
trampling on an enemy who was helpless.

215
00:13:28,200 --> 00:13:34,500
If you want a picture of the future, imagine a boot stamping on a human face forever

216
00:13:34,500 --> 00:13:37,619
He paused as though he expected Winston to speak.

217
00:13:37,619 --> 00:13:41,159
Winston had tried to shrink back into the surface of the bed again.

218
00:13:41,159 --> 00:13:44,939
He could not say anything. His heart seemed to be frozen.

219
00:13:44,939 --> 00:13:49,919
O'Brien went on: 'And remember that it is forever The face

220
00:13:49,919 --> 00:13:51,540
will always be there to be stamped upon.

221
00:13:51,540 --> 00:13:55,860
The heretic, the enemy of society, will always be there, so that he can be

222
00:13:55,860 --> 00:13:58,439
defeated and humiliated over again.

223
00:13:58,439 --> 00:14:02,457
Everything that you have undergone since you have been in our hands— —all that will

224
00:14:02,457 --> 00:14:03,898
continue, and worse.

225
00:14:03,898 --> 00:14:08,279
The espionage that betrayals, the arrests, the tortures, the executions, the

226
00:14:08,279 --> 00:14:12,419
disappearances will never cease. It will be a world of terror as much as a world

227
00:14:12,419 --> 00:14:16,797
of triumph. The more the Party is powerful, the less it will be tolerant:

228
00:14:16,797 --> 00:14:19,919
the weaker the opposition, the tighter the despotism.

229
00:14:19,919 --> 00:14:24,240
Goldstein and his heresies will live forever Every day, at every moment, they

230
00:14:24,240 --> 00:14:28,200
will be defeated, discredited, ridiculed and spat upon— —and yet they will always

231
00:14:28,200 --> 00:14:32,340
survive. This drama that I have played out with you during seven years will be

232
00:14:32,340 --> 00:14:37,680
played out over and over again, generation after generation, always in subtler forms.

233
00:14:37,680 --> 00:14:41,819
Always we shall have the heretic here at our mercy, screaming with pain, broken up,

234
00:14:41,819 --> 00:14:47,520
contemptible— and in the end utterly penitent, saved from himself, crawling to our feet of his

235
00:14:47,520 --> 00:14:48,540
own accord.

236
00:14:48,540 --> 00:14:52,919
That is the world that we are preparing, Winston. A world of victory after victory,

237
00:14:52,919 --> 00:14:58,378
triumph after triumph after triumph: an endless pressing, pressing, pressing upon

238
00:14:58,378 --> 00:14:59,759
the nerve of power.

239
00:14:59,759 --> 00:15:03,599
You are beginning, I can see, to realize what the world will be like.

240
00:15:03,599 --> 00:15:07,619
But in the end you will do more than understand it. You will accept it, welcome

241
00:15:07,619 --> 00:15:10,439
it, become part of it.'

242
00:15:10,439 --> 00:15:13,619
Winston had recovered himself sufficiently to speak.

243
00:15:13,619 --> 00:15:18,898
'You can't!' he said weekly What do you mean by that remark, Winston?'

244
00:15:18,898 --> 00:15:23,099
'You could not create such a world as you have just described. It is a dream.

245
00:15:23,099 --> 00:15:25,080
It is impossible.'

246
00:15:25,080 --> 00:15:26,580
'Why?'

247
00:15:26,580 --> 00:15:30,957
'It is impossible to found a civilization on fear and hatred and cruelty. It would

248
00:15:30,957 --> 00:15:32,099
never endure.'

249
00:15:32,099 --> 00:15:33,957
'Why not?'

250
00:15:33,957 --> 00:15:38,939
'It would have no vitality. It would disintegrate. It would commit suicide.'

251
00:15:38,939 --> 00:15:43,558
'Nonsense. You are under the impression that hatred is more exhausting than love.

252
00:15:43,558 --> 00:15:47,457
Why should it be? And if it were, what difference would that make?

253
00:15:47,457 --> 00:15:51,659
Suppose that we choose to wear ourselves out faster. Suppose that we quicken the

254
00:15:51,659 --> 00:15:54,779
tempo of human life till men are sent out at 30.

255
00:15:54,779 --> 00:15:58,080
Still what difference would it make? Can you not understand that the death of the

256
00:15:58,080 --> 00:16:02,099
individual is not death? The Party is immortal.'

257
00:16:02,099 --> 00:16:06,718
As usual, the voice had battered Winston into helplessness. Moreover he was

258
00:16:06,718 --> 00:16:11,398
injured that if he persisted in his disagreement O'Brien would twist the dial again.

259
00:16:11,398 --> 00:16:15,297
And yet he could not keep silence Feebly, without arguments, with nothing to

260
00:16:15,297 --> 00:16:20,457
support him except his inarticulate horror of what O'Brien had said, he returned to the attack.

261
00:16:20,457 --> 00:16:25,919
'I don't know— —I don't care. Somehow you will fail. Something will defeat you. Life

262
00:16:25,919 --> 00:16:28,378
will defeat you.'

263
00:16:28,378 --> 00:16:31,619
'We control life, Winston, at all its levels.

264
00:16:31,619 --> 00:16:34,558
You are imagining that there is something called human nature which will

265
00:16:34,558 --> 00:16:37,860
be outraged by what we do and will turn against us.

266
00:16:37,860 --> 00:16:41,939
But we create human nature. Men are infinitely malleable.

267
00:16:41,939 --> 00:16:45,659
Or perhaps you have returned to your old idea that the proletarians or the slaves

268
00:16:45,659 --> 00:16:47,759
will arise and overthrow us.

269
00:16:47,759 --> 00:16:52,020
Put it out of your mind. They are helpless, like the animals. Humanity is

270
00:16:52,020 --> 00:16:56,218
the Party. The others are outside— —irrelevant.'

271
00:16:56,218 --> 00:17:00,840
'I don't care. In the end they will beat you. Sooner or later they will see you

272
00:17:00,840 --> 00:17:04,680
for what you are, and then they will tear you to pieces.'

273
00:17:04,680 --> 00:17:09,119
'Do you see any evidence that that is happening? Or any reason why it should?'

274
00:17:09,119 --> 00:17:10,259
'No.

275
00:17:10,259 --> 00:17:11,637
I believe it.

276
00:17:11,637 --> 00:17:15,119
I know that you will fail. There is something in the universe— —I don't know,

277
00:17:15,119 --> 00:17:19,977
some Spirits some principle— —that you will never overcome.'

278
00:17:19,977 --> 00:17:22,259
'Do you believe in God, Winston?'

279
00:17:22,259 --> 00:17:24,240
'No.'

280
00:17:24,240 --> 00:17:27,119
'Then what is it, this principle that will defeat us?'

281
00:17:27,119 --> 00:17:30,540
'I don't know. The spirit of Man.'

282
00:17:30,540 --> 00:17:32,878
'And do you consider yourself a man?'

283
00:17:32,878 --> 00:17:34,558
'Yes.'

284
00:17:34,558 --> 00:17:39,659
'If you are a man, Winston, you are the last man. Your kind is extinct; we are the

285
00:17:39,659 --> 00:17:43,080
inheritors. Do you understand that you are alone?

286
00:17:43,080 --> 00:17:47,939
You are outside history, you are non-existent His manner changed and he said more

287
00:17:47,939 --> 00:17:54,058
harshly: 'And you consider yourself morally superior to us, with our lies and our cruelty?'

288
00:17:54,058 --> 00:17:57,779
'Yes, I consider myself superior.'

289
00:17:57,779 --> 00:18:01,619
O'Brien did not speak. Two other voices were speaking.

290
00:18:01,619 --> 00:18:06,360
After a moment Winston recognized one of them as his own. It was a soundtrack of

291
00:18:06,360 --> 00:18:09,840
the conversation he had had with O'Brien, on the night when he had enrolled

292
00:18:09,840 --> 00:18:14,279
himself in the Brotherhood. He heard himself promising to lie, to steal, to

293
00:18:14,279 --> 00:18:19,259
forge, to murder, to encourage drug taking and prostitution, to disseminate venereal

294
00:18:19,259 --> 00:18:25,797
diseases, to throw vitriol in a child's face her Brian made a small impatient gesture,

295
00:18:25,797 --> 00:18:29,159
as though to say that the demonstration was hardly worth making.

296
00:18:29,159 --> 00:18:32,759
Then he turned a switch and the voices stopped.

297
00:18:32,759 --> 00:18:35,340
'Get up from that bed,' he said.

298
00:18:35,340 --> 00:18:37,919
The bonds had loosened to themselves.

299
00:18:37,919 --> 00:18:41,957
Winston lowered himself to the floor and stood up unsteadily.

300
00:18:41,957 --> 00:18:47,340
'You are the last man,' said O'Brien. 'You are the guardian of the human spirit. You

301
00:18:47,340 --> 00:18:49,080
shall see yourself as you are.

302
00:18:49,080 --> 00:18:51,898
Take off your clothes.'

303
00:18:51,898 --> 00:18:55,378
Winston undid the bit of string that held his overalls together.

304
00:18:55,378 --> 00:18:58,680
The zip fastener had long since been wrenched out of them.

305
00:18:58,680 --> 00:19:02,040
He could not remember whether at any time since his arrest he had taken off

306
00:19:02,040 --> 00:19:04,137
all his clothes at one time.

307
00:19:04,137 --> 00:19:08,520
Beneath the overalls his body was looped with filthy yellowish rags, just

308
00:19:08,520 --> 00:19:13,378
recognizable as the remnants of under clothes As he slid them to the ground he saw

309
00:19:13,378 --> 00:19:16,439
that there was a three-sided mirror at the far end of the room.

310
00:19:16,439 --> 00:19:19,020
He approached it, then stopped short.

311
00:19:19,020 --> 00:19:22,977
An involuntary cry had broken out of him.

312
00:19:22,977 --> 00:19:27,000
'Go on,' said O'Brien. 'Stand between the wings of the mirror. You shall see the

313
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:28,637
side view as well.'

314
00:19:28,637 --> 00:19:31,200
He had stopped because he was frightened.

315
00:19:31,200 --> 00:19:36,898
A bowed Gray colored skeleton-like thing was coming towards him.

316
00:19:36,898 --> 00:19:42,180
Its actual appearance was frightening, and not merely the fact that he knew it to be himself.

317
00:19:42,180 --> 00:19:46,200
He moved closer to the glass. The creature's face seemed to be protruded,

318
00:19:46,200 --> 00:19:48,119
because of its bent carriage.

319
00:19:48,119 --> 00:19:52,500
A forlorn, jailbird's face with a knobby forward running back into a bald scalp, a

320
00:19:52,500 --> 00:19:58,378
crooked nose and battered looking cheekbones above which his eyes were fierce and watchful.

321
00:19:58,378 --> 00:20:01,977
The cheeks were seamed, the mouth had a drawn in look.

322
00:20:01,977 --> 00:20:05,759
Certainly it was his own face, but it seemed to him that it had changed more

323
00:20:05,759 --> 00:20:07,860
than he had changed inside.

324
00:20:07,860 --> 00:20:11,637
The emotions it's registered would be different from the ones he felt.

325
00:20:11,637 --> 00:20:15,718
He had gone partially bald. For the first moment he had thought that he had gone

326
00:20:15,718 --> 00:20:20,040
gray as well, but it was only the scalp that was gray Except for his hands and a

327
00:20:20,040 --> 00:20:25,200
circle of his face, his body was gray all over with ancient, ingrained dirt.

328
00:20:25,200 --> 00:20:29,159
Here and there under the dirt there were the red scars of wounds, and near the

329
00:20:29,159 --> 00:20:33,957
ankle the varicus also was an inflamed mess with flakes of skin peeling off it.

330
00:20:33,957 --> 00:20:37,619
But the truly frightening thing was the emaciation of his body.

331
00:20:37,619 --> 00:20:41,939
The barrel of the ribs was as narrow as that of a skeleton: the legs had shrunk

332
00:20:41,939 --> 00:20:46,137
so that the knees were thicker than the thighs. He saw now what O'Brien had meant

333
00:20:46,137 --> 00:20:47,819
about seeing the side view.

334
00:20:47,819 --> 00:20:51,599
The curvature of the spine was astonishing. The thin shoulders were

335
00:20:51,599 --> 00:20:55,500
hunched forward so as to make a cavity of the chest, the scraggy neck seemed to

336
00:20:55,500 --> 00:20:59,637
be bending double under the weight of the skull and I guess he would have said that it

337
00:20:59,637 --> 00:21:05,119
was the body of a man of sixty, suffering from some malignant disease.

338
00:21:05,398 --> 00:21:09,360
'You have thought sometimes,' said a brand that my face— —the face of a member of the

339
00:21:09,360 --> 00:21:11,520
Inner Party— —looks old and worn.

340
00:21:11,520 --> 00:21:14,340
What do you think of your own face?'

341
00:21:14,340 --> 00:21:18,779
He seized Winston's children spun him around so that he was facing him.

342
00:21:18,779 --> 00:21:22,259
'Look at the condition you were in!' he said. 'Look at this filthy grime all over

343
00:21:22,259 --> 00:21:27,898
your body. Look at the dirt between your toes. Look at that disgusting running sore on your leg.

344
00:21:27,898 --> 00:21:30,360
Do you know that you stink like a goat?

345
00:21:30,360 --> 00:21:32,279
Probably you have ceased to notice it.

346
00:21:32,279 --> 00:21:35,340
Look at your emaciation. Do you see?

347
00:21:35,340 --> 00:21:39,898
I can make my thumb and forefinger meat around your bicep. I could snap your neck

348
00:21:39,898 --> 00:21:41,340
like a carrot.

349
00:21:41,340 --> 00:21:45,000
Do you know that you have lost 25 kilograms since you have been in our

350
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:50,218
hands? Even your hair is coming out in handfuls. Look!' He plucked at Winston's

351
00:21:50,218 --> 00:21:53,099
head and brought away a tuft of hair.

352
00:21:53,099 --> 00:21:57,297
'Open your mouth 9 10 11 teeth left. How

353
00:21:57,297 --> 00:22:00,898
many had you when you came to us? And the few you have left are dropping out of

354
00:22:00,898 --> 00:22:02,700
your head. Look here!'

355
00:22:02,700 --> 00:22:06,000
He seized one of Winston's remaining front teeth between his powerful thumb

356
00:22:06,000 --> 00:22:09,957
and forefinger. A tinge of pain shot through Winston's jaw

357
00:22:09,957 --> 00:22:15,058
Brown had wrenched the loose tooth out by the roots. He tossed it across the cell.

358
00:22:15,058 --> 00:22:19,259
'You were rotting away,' he said; 'you were falling to pieces. What are you? A bag of

359
00:22:19,259 --> 00:22:23,580
filth. Now turn around and look into that mirror again. Do you see that thing

360
00:22:23,580 --> 00:22:28,619
facing you? That is the last man. If you are human, that is humanity.

361
00:22:28,619 --> 00:22:30,898
Now put your clothes on again.'

362
00:22:30,898 --> 00:22:34,619
Winston began to dress himself with slow stiff movements.

363
00:22:34,619 --> 00:22:38,457
Until now he had not seemed to notice how thin and weak he was.

364
00:22:38,457 --> 00:22:41,939
Only one thought stirred in his mind: that he must have been in this place

365
00:22:41,939 --> 00:22:43,919
longer than he had imagined.

366
00:22:43,919 --> 00:22:48,180
Then suddenly as he fixed the miserable rags around himself a feeling of pity

367
00:22:48,180 --> 00:22:50,457
for his ruined body overcame him.

368
00:22:50,457 --> 00:22:54,058
Before he knew what he was doing he had collapsed onto a small stool that stood

369
00:22:54,058 --> 00:22:56,759
beside the bed and burst into tears.

370
00:22:56,759 --> 00:23:00,840
He was aware of his ugliness, his gracelessness, a bundle of bones in

371
00:23:00,840 --> 00:23:04,020
filthy under clothes sitting weeping in the harsh white light:

372
00:23:04,020 --> 00:23:09,840
but he could not stop himself. O'Brien laid a hand on his shoulder, almost kindly.

373
00:23:09,840 --> 00:23:13,319
'It will not last forever he said. 'You can escape from it whenever you choose.

374
00:23:13,319 --> 00:23:15,898
Everything depends on yourself.'

375
00:23:15,898 --> 00:23:20,398
'You did it!' sobbed Winston. 'You reduced me to this state.'

376
00:23:20,398 --> 00:23:22,439
'No, Winston, you reduced yourself to it.

377
00:23:22,439 --> 00:23:26,218
This is what you accepted when you set yourself up against the Party.

378
00:23:26,218 --> 00:23:28,080
It was all contained in that first act.

379
00:23:28,080 --> 00:23:31,740
Nothing has happened that you did not foresee.'

380
00:23:31,740 --> 00:23:36,058
He paused, and then went on: 'We have beaten you, Winston. We have

381
00:23:36,058 --> 00:23:40,137
broken you up. You have seen what your body is like. Your mind is in the same

382
00:23:40,137 --> 00:23:44,398
state. I do not think that there can be much pride left in you. You have been

383
00:23:44,398 --> 00:23:48,000
kicked and flogged and insulted, you have screamed with pain, you have rolled on

384
00:23:48,000 --> 00:23:50,218
the floor in your own blood and vomit.

385
00:23:50,218 --> 00:23:53,939
You have whimpered for mercy, you have betrayed everybody and everything. Can

386
00:23:53,939 --> 00:23:57,360
you think of a single degradation that has not happened to you?'

387
00:23:57,360 --> 00:24:01,020
Winston had stopped weeping, though the tears were still losing out of his eyes.

388
00:24:01,020 --> 00:24:03,659
He looked up at O'Brien.

389
00:24:03,659 --> 00:24:06,718
'I have not betrayed Julia,' he said.

390
00:24:06,718 --> 00:24:09,419
O'Brien looked down at him thoughtfully.

391
00:24:09,419 --> 00:24:13,080
'No,' he said, 'no; that is perfectly true.

392
00:24:13,080 --> 00:24:15,540
You have not betrayed Julia.'

393
00:24:15,540 --> 00:24:19,740
The peculiar reverence for O'Brien, which nothing seemed able to destroy, flooded

394
00:24:19,740 --> 00:24:21,599
Winston's heart again.

395
00:24:21,599 --> 00:24:24,360
How intelligent, he thought, how intelligent!

396
00:24:24,360 --> 00:24:27,898
Never did O'Brien fail to understand what was said to him.

397
00:24:27,898 --> 00:24:32,099
Anyone else on earth would have answered promptly that he had to betrayed Julia.

398
00:24:32,099 --> 00:24:35,939
For what was there that they had not screwed out of him under that torture?

399
00:24:35,939 --> 00:24:40,020
He had told them everything he knew about her, her habits, her character, her

400
00:24:40,020 --> 00:24:44,159
past life; he had confessed in the most trivial detail everything that had

401
00:24:44,159 --> 00:24:48,058
happened at their meetings, all that he had said to her and she to him, their

402
00:24:48,058 --> 00:24:53,700
black market meals, their adulteries, their vague plottings against the Party— —everything.

403
00:24:53,700 --> 00:24:57,957
And yet, in the sense in which he intended the word, he had not betrayed her.

404
00:24:57,957 --> 00:25:02,939
He had not stopped loving her; his feelings towards her had remained the same

405
00:25:02,939 --> 00:25:06,860
Brian had seen what he meant without the need for explanation.

406
00:25:06,860 --> 00:25:10,797
'Tell me,' he said, 'how soon will they shoot me?'

407
00:25:10,797 --> 00:25:15,599
'It might be a long time,' said O'Brien. 'You are a difficult case. But don't give up

408
00:25:15,599 --> 00:25:17,700
hope. Everyone is cured sooner or later.

409
00:25:17,700 --> 00:25:20,000
In the end we shall shoot you
